# Commit on main

When a dots change should persist, apply it on the main checkout at `~/dots`, on `main`, and commit there. A commit that exists only on a linked worktree branch is easy to miss, because `~/dots` is the live tree. If you edited a worktree first, apply the same patch on `~/dots` and commit it there, then restore the worktree so it does not look like a second uncommitted change.

A worktree commit is allowed if Drew asks for that branch. This rule is only for this repo.
